# Conventions

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|----|----|----|
| File | `kebab-case.ts` | `claude-code-adapter.ts` |
| Directory | `kebab-case` | `adapter-sdk/`, `claude-code/` |
| Function / variable | `camelCase` | `parseJsonlLine`, `storageRoot` |
| Type / interface / class | `PascalCase` | `MemoryRecord`, `IBaseAdapter` |
| Interface prefix | `I` for SDK contracts only | `IBaseAdapter`, `IIdeAdapter` (pattern matches existing SDK) |
| Constant (module-level frozen) | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `DEFAULT_DENYLIST`, `MAX_LINE_BYTES` |
| Test file | `<source>.test.ts` | `scan.test.ts` |
| Bun script | `kebab-case.ts` | `scripts/version-bump.ts` |

## Imports

- **Top of file only.** No inline `await import()` except in dynamic plugin loading (M4+).
- **Type imports**: `import type { X } from '...'` when only types are used.
- **Order**: external first, then `@oh-my-memories/*`, then relative. Biome's `organizeImports` enforces.
- **Workspace deps**: import from `@oh-my-memories/<pkg>`, never `../../../other-pkg/src`.

## Comments

- Comments explain **why**, never **what**.
- ❌ `// Increment counter`
- ❌ `// Define the function`
- ✅ `// Skip records older than 90 days; keeps recall result set < 1k for default queries`
- ✅ `// JSONL files >100MB exist (long CC sessions); stream line-by-line to keep RAM bounded`

## TypeScript

- **Strict mode is on.** Don't disable.
- **No `any`** without `// biome-ignore lint/suspicious/noExplicitAny: <reason>` on the same line.
- **Prefer `unknown`** over `any` when the value comes from outside (`JSON.parse`, network).
- **Return types on exported functions** are explicit. Inferred returns OK for internal.
- **Errors**: throw `Error` subclass with a meaningful name (`AdapterDetectError`, `CorruptRecordError`). No `throw "string"`.

## Async

- **`async`/`await`**, not `.then()`.
- **`AsyncIterable`** for streaming (adapters' `scan()`).
- **`Promise.all`** when iterations are independent. Sequential `await` only when there's a dependency.
- **No floating promises.** Either `await`, `void`, or pass to `Promise.all`.

## Errors and exit codes

CLI exit codes:
- `0` — success
- `1` — generic error (parse failure, unexpected exception)
- `2` — bad CLI arg (parsing the user's command line)
- `3` — adapter detection failed (no sources found)
- `4` — IO error (permission denied, etc.)
- `5` — partial success with errors (some adapters worked, some failed)

JSON error shape (when `--json`):
```json
{ "ok": false, "error": { "code": "ADAPTER_DETECT_FAILED", "message": "...", "details": {} } }
```

## Cross-platform

- **Paths**: always `node:path` (`join`, `resolve`). Never string-concat with `/`.
- **Home**: `os.homedir()`. Never `process.env.HOME` (Windows).
- **Line endings**: write files with `\n`. Read tolerantly (`\r\n` OK).
- **Case**: filesystem case-sensitivity differs. Normalize to lowercase before string compares on adapter IDs.

## Performance budgets (soft, M1)

- `omem scan` finishes in <2s on a typical machine (10k records across 4 adapters)
- `omem recall --all "<word>"` finishes in <500ms after first run (cache warms after scan)
- CLI startup overhead <50ms (Bun cold start)
- No single in-memory data structure exceeds 100MB during scan

## Commits

- Conventional Commits: `feat: ...`, `fix: ...`, `docs: ...`, `refactor: ...`, `test: ...`, `chore: ...`
- Subject ≤72 chars
- Body explains *why*, not *what*
